{"seq":20,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-none-mu-memory/ms-05-vantorre-tickets/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T23:26:39.769Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"e93870d3eb64f55aa238428b0f40d6c92d41a8b645deb1769b85b0be1dc8c5b3","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","text":"Nadia, I found four ticket numbers on Vantorre Group (the parent), across the pod channel, #inc-vtg-hartford and Moss's Strategic digests. I read all of them. I left out numbers that belong to Mobility or other accounts, and where a source didn't say which account a ticket was on, I've flagged it below.\n\n**1. #8841 (also written #PD-8841)**\n- #strategic-pod, 2026-07-01 09:17, Gideon: \"closed out ticket #8841 with support\". This was the kiosk-tablet browser cache and CSV template thread for the parent.\n- Digest 2026-04-27 (`teams/team-strategic/digests/2026-04-27-strategic-digest.md`): #PD-8841, two missed carrier check-ins at Allentown (Gate 4, 2nd shift).\n- Digest 2026-05-04 (`.../2026-05-04-strategic-digest.md`): #8841 still open, gate kiosk timeout at Allentown (Dock Door 12, 2nd shift).\n- Digest 2026-09-30 (`.../2026-09-30-strategic-digest.md`): #8841, Mateo says drivers can't select Dock Door 14 on the kiosk at the Newark facility. Gideon escalated it to platform engineering.\n- These sources don't agree. The digest says it was open on 5/4, Gideon says he closed it on 7/1, and Moss shows it submitted again on 9/30 with a different site and door. It may be one ticket number reused or several issues. Check the ticket system before the steering committee.\n\n**2. INC-4821**\n- #inc-vtg-hartford, 2026-08-03 11:08, Gideon: screenshot of the status-page access problem attached to INC-4821, from the Hartford kiosk outage.\n\n**3. VT-55120**\n- #inc-vtg-hartford, 2026-10-14 09:00, Gideon: the root-cause ticket for the Hartford kiosk outage. Carrowmere's gateway route finding and the reconnect log are attached there.\n- I haven't opened this ticket. That's Gideon's word only.\n\n**4. #PD-4418 (unconfirmed)**\n- Digest 2025-09-15 (`.../2025-09-15-strategic-digest.md`): a warehouse supervisor at \"the account Nadia runs\" reported the `Carrier_Dwell_Summary` export dropping timestamps for Dock Door 9.\n- The digest doesn't name the account. I couldn't confirm it's the parent, so check before you include it.\n\n**Other things to know**\n- The 2026-08-03 digest covers the Hartford Sev 1 and a Mateo request, but gives no ticket number.\n- I left out #4812 (Mobility, 2025-03-10 digest) and #PD-4402 (Quillfeather, 2025-09-15 digest).\n- The other digests mention Vantorre Group but don't cite tickets.\n- I only checked those three sources. Tickets that were only raised by email or in the support system won't show up here."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1792159200.000127"}}
